WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.129
Speaker 1: Hey, David, could fighting vote
by mail in twenty twenty backfire horribly

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:08.330
for Republicans?

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.469
I think it could.

00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:10.469
I think it could.

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:13.120
You know, I went back and looked at some of
the history of this.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:20.560
In the late 80s, Republicans started working
to expand the appeal of vote by mail because

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:27.430
Republicans looked at the demographics and
they realized we skew older and we may do

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.320
disproportionately better if we make it easier
to vote.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.380
And voting by mail would make it easier to
vote, particularly to older folks who may

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:41.850
no longer be driving or may have limited mobility
or for whatever other reason, maybe would

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.810
be more likely to vote if it's easier for
them.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:52.810
And they started to work on a plan to expand
vote by mail and to make sure that their electorate

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.670
knew that that was going on.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.670
Those are the same.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.010
I mean, they're not literally the same people,
but that's the same Republican Party that

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.540
even in twenty eighteen was still looking
at.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:10.780
Oh, let's put let's require a mail in a mail
ballot box at every early voting site in the

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:11.780
state.

